00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:06.710 align:start position:0%
european fisheries ministers have  reached an agreement on fishing  opportunities for next year for certain  stocks in eu and some non-eu waters  increasing the number of sustainably  managed stocks this annual process is  based on recommendations from the  european commission taking into account  scientific advice it concerns stocks in  the atlantic the north sea international  fishing where eu vessels take part and  in the black sea the best news is that  we have also succeeded in increasing the  number of stocks that are now managed at  sustainable levels and i can therefore  say that sustainably many stocks are now  abroadly accepted concept across  the european union  fishing opportunity limits are aimed at  keeping stock sustainable they take the  form of total allowable catches or tax  for each stock and each fishing zone  tax are then divided into quotas between  member states  the commission has also briefed  ministers on the way the fish landing  obligations being implemented the rules  are part of recent reform to the common  fishing policy and they'll enter force  in january to ensure that less fish are  thrown away  on farm issues the italian presidency  reported on progress made on legislative  proposals for organic farming the school  fruit vegetable and milk scheme official  controls and plant health agriculture  ministers also looked at challenges to  the dairy sector given price volatility  and the impact of the russian ban in  europe on dairy produce many member  states also supported presidency plans  to strengthen eu policies for young  farmers
 

